# acc.add_product(x, y) of Accumulator<T, 1> (milestone2.md, "The accumulator"): the running sum s
# plus the exact product x y, rounded once (the step of dot_1, s <- RN(x y + s)), and the running sum
# a of the magnitudes plus |x| |y|, rounded once (a <- RN(|x| |y| + a)). x and y are values of the
# program that are only multiplied: rule R3 asks no guard of them.
#
# The claims proposed for it in gen/kernels, which accumulator.py checks:
#   value:         s+x*y
#   requires:      nonneg a
#   ensures:       rounded t nearest
#   ensures:       rounded b nearest value=a+abs(x)*abs(y)
#   (needs rounded ... value=, which the generator does not have: see accumulator.py)
kernel:        acc_mul_1
input:         stored s
input:         stored a
input:         x
input:         y
output:        t
output:        b
min_precision: 1
source:        the step of the fused dot product of one limb, and the sum of the magnitudes (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   b, the sum of magnitudes, does not reach t; it overflows (to +inf, its operands being nonnegative) only when a + |x| |y| rounds above the largest number of T, and a radius computed from it is then +inf, the whole line

t  = fma(x, y, s)
ax = abs(x)
ay = abs(y)
b  = fma(ax, ay, a)
